  -o /tmp/mr3160_kernel > ~/mr3160_dump.log 2>&1
echo "exit: $?"
du -sh ~/mr3160_dump.log
```

Then the counts:

```bash
grep -cE 'hivm\.multi_buffer = 2|annotation\.mark.*multi_buffer' ~/mr3160_dump.log
grep -cE 'arith\.select.*memref<.*#hivm\.address_space<ub>' ~/mr3160_dump.log
grep -c "annotatedDynamicBound\|PassID" ~/mr3160_dump.log
```

Note the kernel from that dump hash is the B4-T1024 case, which you already established is healthy at 826us. If the task targets a different kernel, use that one instead. `ls /root/.triton/dump/` on the A5 has 3.9G of them, so match the hash to the case you actually care about.
